    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1364">

                <pb facs="1621" n="1423" xml:id="pg1423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"><hi rendition="#small-caps">SWNCC
                    Files</hi></note>
                <head>No. 1364<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee
                        to Members of the Committee Panel at Babelsberg</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1364-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-18">18 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <table>
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell rendition="#top #nowrap"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum
                                for</hi>:</cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Dunn</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. McCloy</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#small-caps">Admiral Gardner</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: United States Policy Regarding Dardanelles and Kiel
                    Canal</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">References: JCS 1418 Series<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1364-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>The attached memorandum to the Secretary of State,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1364-f3"
                    /> embodying a report by the Joint Chiefs of Staff on recommended U. S. policy
                    concerning the Dardanelles and the Kiel Canal,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d1364-f4"/>
                    is circulated for informal consideration.</p>
                <p>It is requested that you indicate your concurrence or comments.</p>
                <closer>For the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee[:]<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">H A Gerhardt</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colonel, G. S. C. Acting Secretary</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">S. W. N. C</hi>. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >C</hi>.]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1364-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1364-f1-content">
                <p>Gardner indicated his approval of the attachment to this memorandum on July 18.
                    Dunn signed his copy, giving his approval, but did not indicate the date. For
                    McCloy’s comment, see <ref target="#d1365">document No. 1365</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1364-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1364-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. Cf. <ref target="#d1363">document No. 1363</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1364-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1364-f3-content">
                <p>See the attachment to <ref target="#d1365">document No. 1365</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1364-f4" n="4" xml:id="d1364-f4-content">
                <p><ref target="#d751">Documents Nos. 751</ref> and <ref target="#d1363"
                    >1363</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
